/E (Association of Indian Universities \(AIU\), New Delhi, the world's largest association of universities and a premier apex body in higher education in India in collaboration with National Institute of Technology Karnataka \(NITK\), Surathkal, an Institute of National Importance and one of India's top 20 engineering institutions \(NIRF 2025\), ranked 120th among universities in Southern Asia \(QS World University Rankings 2024\), is organising the South Zone Conference on "Strategic Integration of Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) in Higher Education: Opportunities, Challenges and Implications" on 18 September 2026 \(Friday\). The conference aims to provide a vibrant platform for academicians, administrators, industry experts, and other stakeholders to deliberate on the strategic integration of AI in higher education. It seeks to encourage speakers and delegates to share best practices adopted within)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [28]
